 opposes the existing magnetic field and the current flows from left to right in the straight wire, that is, along the hypotenuse current. That is, there is a repulsive force between the wire and the loop.\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Electromagnetic Induction Question 19 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n<br>Also, if the loop is rotated about the wire, there is no change in the flux through the wire, so no extra induced emf is generated in the wire.","exam":"jee-advanced","questions":[{"question_id":"a-conducting-loop-in-the-shape-of-a-right-angled-isosceles-t-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-gs4gjqg8klruxiwc","qKey":"a-conducting-loop-in-the-shape-of-a-right-angled-isosceles-t-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-gs4gjqg8klruxiwc","permalink":"a-conducting-loop-in-the-shape-of-a-right-angled-isosceles-t-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-gs4gjqg8klruxiwc","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 1 Offline","year":2016,"subject":"physics","chapter":"electromagnetic-induction","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":2,"content":"A conducting loop in the shape of a right angled isosceles triangle of height 10 cm is kept such that the 90<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 436.6 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> vertex is very close to an infinitely long conducting wire (see the figure). The wire is electrically insulated from the loop. The hypotenuse of the triangle is parallel to the wire. The current in the triangular loop is in counterclockwise direction and increased at a constant rate of 10 As<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-