 creates it. Since the flux is increasing, the induced emf opposes the existing magnetic field and the current flows from left to right in the straight wire, that is, along the hypotenuse current. That is, there is a repulsive force between the wire and the loop.\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Electromagnetic Induction Question 19 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1li3668ri/4f956045-fb87-4532-a7b9-2945be57e31c/01204fe0-fb00-11ed-8333-f921c26ec676/file-1li3668rj.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n<br>Also, if the loop is rotated about the wire, there is no change in the flux through the wire, so no extra induced emf is generated in the wire.","exam":"jee-advanced"}]}